{"artifacts":[],"cancelled_at":null,"effects":[],"expected_sha":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","generation":6,"intent":{"claim":"47cea49310654661b37feec7b9be9677","dispatch_status":"acknowledged","id":"da4fee65cca84dc3a534608f734603b6","recorded_at":1791442436},"iteration":1,"next_check_at":1791443091,"phase":"e9ded454c6b64c208a13c6a22dfd6509","publications":[],"reason":null,"report":null,"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5437480598,5437827324,5437827889,5437849721,5447128387,5448100472,5448112907,5448217030,5451619668,5451663393],"budgets":{"deadline_seconds":7200,"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"deadline":1791449634,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nEmpty Spring selectors override Logback XML configuration, and empty structured keys can drop log records.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Filter empty structured attribute keys before OpenTelemetry capture](#discussion_r4214926202) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Preserve empty selector to honor Logback XML attribute filters](#discussion_r4214926310) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Skip empty map keys before creating OpenTelemetry attributes](#discussion_r4211861168)\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5451663393","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5451663393},{"body":"[General] Structured capture now defaults to all, so empty keys supplied through SLF4J key-value pairs or Logstash markers reach `captureAttribute`. OpenTelemetry rejects empty attribute names, causing that log record to be dropped instead of merely omitting the invalid structured entry. Filter empty keys in the shared structured selector before any structured source is processed.","comment_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","comment_id":4214926202,"key":"inline:4214926202","kind":"inline","line":82,"original_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","original_line":82,"path":"instrumentation/logback/logback-appender-1.0/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/logback/appender/v1_0/internal/LoggingEventMapper.java","review_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","review_id":5451663393,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T05:00:29Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"205ddc83433e42464d54e51f411a8007e18ee585d67ec61faa5d9668939e4aec","id":4214926202,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T05:00:29Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qNFvr"},{"body":"[Config] Converting an absent or empty common selector into an explicit `included=[\"*\"]` selector makes it override `structuredAttributesIncluded` / `structuredAttributesExcluded` declared in `logback.xml`. For example, a Spring application with `<structuredAttributesExcluded>*</structuredAttributesExcluded>` and no corresponding Spring property will unexpectedly capture everything. Preserve an empty selector here so the appender can fall back to its XML selector and only use the capture-all default when both sources are empty.","comment_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","comment_id":4214926310,"key":"inline:4214926310","kind":"inline","line":32,"original_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","original_line":32,"path":"instrumentation/spring/spring-boot-autoconfigure/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/spring/autoconfigure/internal/instrumentation/logging/StructuredAttributesConfig.java","review_commit_id":"cd6a4376389ce9a99cac6583a227995cdf7b7da0","review_id":5451663393,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T05:00:29Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"d468136752f1c0e4d89fad407ceceb9dc4980d0ba3805e9a60509a056a87be1b","id":4214926310,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T05:00:29Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qNFwi"}],"frozen_at":1791442434,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-0